export const title = "Arm / Disarm Setup Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Arm / Disarm Setup Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n      <p>Disarm settings let you control whether actions fire when an event occurs.</p>\n\n      <h2>Disarm Overview</h2>\n      <p>While disarmed, actions do not fire even if an event occurs. Besides the setting available on the web page, the state can also be changed using an <strong>alarm input</strong>, a <strong>schedule</strong>, and other methods.</p>\n      <p>The <span style=\"display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;\">Arm/Disarm <span style=\"background:#2653d6;border-radius:10px;width:34px;height:18px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"><span style=\"position:absolute;right:2px;top:2px;width:14px;height:14px;background:#fff;border-radius:50%;\"></span></span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Arm</span></span> button in the top header changes the device's global disarm state.</p>\n      <p>If <strong>Run rule while disarmed</strong> is checked in the rule condition settings, the action still fires even while the device is disarmed.</p>\n\n      <h2>Global Disarm</h2>\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n        <div class=\"app-panel\">\n          <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n            <span>Linked to Alarm IN</span>\n            <select disabled><option>None</option><option>Alarm In 1</option><option>Alarm In 2</option><option>Alarm In 3</option></select>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption>Global disarm \u2014 link to an alarm input</figcaption>\n      </div>\n      <p>The selected alarm input's state is kept in sync with the global disarm state.</p>\n      <p>If linked to an alarm input, the disarm state can't be changed from the web page or via the API.</p>\n\n      <h2>Instant Disarm Settings</h2>\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:600px;\">\n        <div class=\"app-panel\">\n          <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:10px;\">Disarm Status (Arm/Disarm) &nbsp; <span style=\"color:var(--green);\">&#9679;1 &#9679;2 &#9679;3 &#9679;4</span> &nbsp; <span class=\"btn small\">System Event Action Rule</span></div>\n          <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:16px;\">Alarm In &nbsp; <span style=\"color:var(--green);\">&#9679;1 &#9679;2 &#9679;3 &#9679;4</span></div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px;font-size:12px;\">\n            <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">All</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n            <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">CH 1</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n            <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">CH 2</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n            <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">CH 3</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"margin-top:14px;font-size:12px;\">\n            <div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">System Event Action Rule</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption>Instant arm/disarm settings</figcaption>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n        <p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:700;\">&#8251; Disarm Composition</p>\n        <ul class=\"steps\" style=\"margin:0;\">\n          <li><strong>Global</strong> &ndash; configured from the top header of the UI, and controls whether actions fire across the entire device. Takes priority over both the per-channel setting and the system action rule disarm setting.</li>\n          <li><strong>All</strong> &ndash; sets the firing state for every channel and configured action at once.</li>\n          <li><strong>Per-channel</strong> &ndash; sets whether actions fire when an event occurs on the selected channel.</li>\n          <li><strong>System Event Action Rule</strong> &ndash; sets whether actions configured under system events/actions fire.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>In the instant arm/disarm settings, use the buttons to set the state of <strong>All</strong>, <strong>per-channel</strong>, and <strong>system event actions</strong> individually.</p>\n      <p>If the global disarm state is set to disarm, event actions do not fire regardless of the per-channel arm state.</p>\n\n      <h2>Disarm Rule Settings</h2>\n      <p>From the disarm settings screen, click the button in the <strong>Disarm Rule Settings</strong> area to add a rule.</p>\n\n      <h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Alarm Input</h3>\n      <p>You can configure a rule using a specific alarm input.</p>\n\n      <h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Schedule</h3>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Enter a name in <strong>Rule Name</strong> to distinguish this rule.</li>\n        <li>The <strong>Enable</strong> toggle sets whether the rule is active.</li>\n        <li><strong>Rule Handler</strong> sets whether this rule is an alarm-input rule or a schedule rule.</li>\n        <li><strong>Disarm Status Setting</strong> sets whether the rule sets the state to arm or disarm when it fires.</li>\n        <li><strong>Arm/Disarm Target</strong> selects what the rule applies to.</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p>You can configure a schedule to change the disarm state.</p>\n      <p>Set the target days and specify a time window to configure the schedule. For example, you could configure a rule that disarms every Saturday at 00:00.</p>";
